Based on the council's outbuilding guidance, a garden shed under 2.5 metres high usually does not need a planning application, provided:

- It is behind the front wall of the house.
- It covers less than half of the garden.

Please note:

- **Conservation areas and listed buildings are different.** If your property is in one, you may need to apply even for a small shed.
- If your shed is on the front of the property, is taller than 2.5 metres, or would cover more than half the garden, an application is likely needed.

If you give me your property address, I can check whether it has any constraints (such as a conservation area or listed building status). I can't give a formal opinion on your specific proposal. If you're unsure, the council's planning team can confirm whether you need to apply before you start.
